{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons","id":1479222,"title":"[Dragon] Scent the Divine & Dragons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-21T01:35:24-07:00","id":1479222,"title":"[Dragon] Scent the Divine & Dragons?","content":"<b>How general Knack for all Scion characters - <i>Scent the Divine</i> - works on Dragons?</b><br /> Bonus questions - <b>How would it work on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1447969-reptilians-and-dinosaurs?p=1450481#post1450481\">Reptilians Infiltrators</a> - would their clone skin shield them?</b> How would Reptilians smell like? ( In my games, Reptilians are helping Dragons in reptiles Great Plan... )<br /> <br /> Knacks general text:<br /> <i>'<b>Scent the Divine:</b> Having a touch of divinity, the Scion has an innate sense of anything divine near him. With a sniff or a knowing listen, he can detect another Scion of a particular pantheon.'</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/j3YYixA.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/MmqxMBq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/o6s5Sk2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ib23dP1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-21-2022, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T11:54:29-07:00","id":1479254,"title":"","content":"By the wording of the Knack, it only works on Scions, not Heirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T11:19:56-07:00","id":1479433,"title":"","content":"The draft of Dragon that backers received has revised text that explicitly includes heirs and dragons, and iirc they add that if an old knack is included in Dragon, it can be considered unofficial errata if its text differs from previous versions.<br /> <br /> So yes, by default a Scion should probably be able to detect an heir, although given their secretive nature it shouldn't be terribly clear what they've noticed.<br /> <br /> As for the reptilians, I would argue that the knack can detect them by default, but some may have a skin that provides greater protection, or some other means of avoiding it.<br /> <br /> I can't say what sensory impressions they would leave; that plays into their cultural motifs and I don't know that at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T18:16:12-07:00","id":1479458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479433#post1479433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The draft of Dragon that backers received has revised text that explicitly includes heirs and dragons, and iirc they add that if an old knack is included in Dragon, it can be considered unofficial errata if its text differs from previous versions.<br /> <br /> So yes, by default a Scion should probably be able to detect an heir, although given their secretive nature it shouldn't be terribly clear what they've noticed..</div> </div> </div> </div>So ALL scions and dragons have Scent the Divine for free? Or just they all CAN BUY the Scent Knack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T18:26:55-07:00","id":1479460,"title":"","content":"\u201cAt Inheritance 1, every Heir gains the ability to Scent the Divine.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T19:18:30-07:00","id":1479462,"title":"","content":"Scions do still have to buy it, although they do get it for free at Demigod if they haven't already.<br /> <br /> When I said &quot;by default, etc&quot;, I meant that a Scion who had scent the divine could use it to detect dragons and their kind in the rules as written, but I also know that your preferred style of play makes things harder on the children and champions of gods, so your own rulings might vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T14:16:56-07:00","id":1479505,"title":"","content":"One must ask then what dragons would smell like. I imagine something spicy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T14:23:13-07:00","id":1479507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479505#post1479505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One must ask then what dragons would smell like. I imagine something spicy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Dragons Scent be based on their Flight? My propositions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Draqs</b> \u2013 Hot, dry air - like on desert<br /> \u2022 <b>Joka </b>\u2013 Smell of savanah?<br /> \u2022 <b>Lindwurms</b> \u2013 Smell of deep sea?<br /> \u2022 <b>L\u00f3ng </b>\u2013 Smell of fresh river - coming across Asia<br /> \u2022 <b>Naga</b> \u2013 Smell of high mountains ( like Himalaya )?<br /> \u2022 <b>Serpents</b> \u2013 Smell of tropical jungle - from where Serpents come","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2022, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T16:55:16-07:00","id":1479515,"title":"","content":"It does indeed depend on Flight. Though if there's a box in there describing what each Flight smells like, I'm having trouble finding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T18:33:43-07:00","id":1479522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479462#post1479462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions do still have to buy it, although they do get it for free at Demigod if they haven't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you confirm where is this from? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T18:49:57-07:00","id":1479525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479522#post1479522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you confirm where is this from? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Hero (and Origin), Scent of the Divine is described as any other knack, and so should be considered as so.<br /> <br /> In Demigod, it is explicitly described that Demigods gain the Scent of the Divine for free if they don\u2019t have it yet.<br /> <br /> In Dragon it is described they all have the Scent of the Divine Knack for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T19:17:15-07:00","id":1479526,"title":"","content":"In addition, Dragon also contrasts the \u201cHeirs get it automatically\u201d with an \u201c\u2026unlike Scions.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T07:18:53-07:00","id":1479653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479433#post1479433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the reptilians, I would argue that the knack can detect them by default, but some may have a skin that provides greater protection, or some other means of avoiding it.<br /> <br /> I can't say what sensory impressions they would leave; that plays into their cultural motifs and I don't know that at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, with Dragons secretive nature and Reptilians false skin - they have Difficulty 2 for uncovering their identity by Scent the Divine? Or maybe higher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-28-2022, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T11:54:36-07:00","id":1479662,"title":"","content":"I think its supposed to work in a 'secretive dragons aren't going to be in the same room as a Scion unless they <i>want </i>to interact' kind of way, maybe? Actually, this does bring up a larger point, how does scent of the divine work with stealth or disguise attempts in general? Is it just impossible to mask your scent in any way so that you can pass off as mortal to someone who has it if you are trying to be a sneaky manipulative person tricking them into doing something for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T13:08:08-07:00","id":1479665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1479653#post1479653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, with Dragons secretive nature and Reptilians false skin - they have Difficulty 2 for uncovering their identity by Scent the Divine? Or maybe higher?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see dragons having a specific resistance to it. They're secretive by necessity, not by immutable nature.<br /> <br /> As for the knack itself, there's not a roll attached to it, just the need for a Scion to actively decide to use it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd take a different tack if I were to do this. The Reptilians have no especial defense against being detected. But they have qualities that scramble the signal such that a Scion has no idea where this strange, hissing susurrus of prehuman voices originates from. It could be anyone, or even any number of people. You might be surrounded and just now realizing it. Or maybe there's just the one. You just know you aren't alone.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they automatically realize you've sounded them out.<br /> <br /> Possibly both. <br /> <br /> I just feel like there should be other ways to play with player paranoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 04-29-2022, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T12:12:15-07:00","id":1479729,"title":"","content":"So, on doing a bit of rereading, the Demigod book has some things whose mystical ability is throwing off attempts to recognize their divine nature via Scent the Divine (EX: The Iron Leaf of Hel lets you throw it off alongside being good for doing liminal things) . So presumably a dragon who wants to be near a scion without being noticed as a dragon needs to get some magic going or grab an artifact to counter it and can't do so via mundane means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T20:44:02-07:00","id":1481274,"title":"","content":"Kinda late for this topic but i would like to add my view on this case, on dragon manuscript Scent of divine is trated like a innate power not a knack, so i think the thing on knacks part who gives permission to use more updated knacks wont work here.<br /> <br /> Bem-sucedida Scion Dragon is a game about spys, secrets and etc, i really think scions instant blow the heirs covers a lot anti climatic, the manuscript goes even further giving us mechanics on transformations who may \u201cblow\u201d the cover.<br /> <br /> On my games i dont let scent of divine reach heirs, if a heirs is exposed its usually because of their lack of good sense, and usually a Scion will probably see him as a monster and try build his legend on killing him (of course some pantheonsclike the Orix\u00e1s wont, but the general Scion consensus is Dragon and their spawn are bad guys).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T12:37:12-07:00","id":1481395,"title":"","content":"So, from the answer I received in the ask a line dev topic, it seems the answer is that a dragon who wants to interact with a scion who has scent the divine without being outed needs to get some sort of supernatural power of concealment. Which seems fair, if the other person is going to invest XP into being able to find divine beings then you should have to spend XP on thwarting them.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, just learn to work through proxies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T10:33:34-07:00","id":1481465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1481395#post1481395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, from the answer I received in the ask a line dev topic, it seems the answer is that a dragon who wants to interact with a scion who has scent the divine without being outed needs to get some sort of supernatural power of concealment. Which seems fair, if the other person is going to invest XP into being able to find divine beings then you should have to spend XP on thwarting them.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, just learn to work through proxies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agre on Dragon using proxies, the main problem here is with Heirs ,their dont have usually that much proxies to use.<br /> <br /> On exp cost, Demi-gods actually get the Scent of divine for free, also Heirs get \u201cmodest human guise\u201d, wich would make a clash of wills i believe and thats totally fine.<br /> <br /> The main issue for me is scent of divine as described on Dragon is not a \u201cknack\u201d is a natural power for Heirs ( it dont even take a knack active slot) and it is a lot diferent of scions version ( on hero it is a knack and only ler you motive things related to pantheons if i recall well), so i think scions should stick with \u201ctheir\u201d version of scent of divine, i think it make more sense lore wise, hope we get more on this on Dragon final drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T11:17:08-07:00","id":1481468,"title":"","content":"True, I forgot that for a second. I guess then you could houserule dragons as automatically getting a stealth power once they hit their version of demi-god?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T04:47:41-07:00","id":1481522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1481468#post1481468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, I forgot that for a second. I guess then you could houserule dragons as automatically getting a stealth power once they hit their version of demi-god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that can be done, or we can make the dragonic knack \u201cModest Human guise\u201d, makes a clash of wills on scent on divine, the words on manuscript dont give that much detail on it just saying it gives \u201c +1 Dificult \u201c to detect.<br /> <br /> \u201cModest Human Guise: This Knack requires activation at the start of the scene. For the duration of the scene, suppress all transformed Knacks and return to your ordinary human form. Anyone seeking out magical creatures suffers a +1 Difficulty to notice you while this Knack is active. Modest Human Guise cannot be Transformed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Since it seems one power counter another i would probably make a clash of wills giving + 1 enchancement for the Heir, then probably it will be fair for both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T06:51:09-07:00","id":1481531,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T06:46:17-07:00","id":1481917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1481531#post1481531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found more information on Dragon Manuscript, it seems Heirs Scent of Divine is really different from scions at least if we go on what is writen.<br /> <br /> \u201c Scent the Divine<br /> At Inheritance 1, every Heir gains the ability to Scent the Divine. Unlike Heroes, whose senses have been dulled by their human nature, Heirs are keenly aware of the supernatural around them. All Heirs have the following ability: Scent the Divine: Knowing the smell of your kin, you have an innate sense of anything supernatural or divine near you. With a sniff or a knowing listen, you may detect another Heir or Dragon (or Scion, God, or Legendary Creature, etc.) of a particular Flight.\u201c<br /> <br /> On Scions we have: \u201cScent the Divine: Having a touch of divinity, you have an innate sense of anything divine near you. With a sniff or a knowing listen, you may detect an- other Scion (or God, or Legendary Creature, etc.) of a particular pantheon.\u201d<br /> <br /> It seems the \u201c sense dulled \u201c on dragon manuscript cover this one, so it seems a Scion would no be able to sense a Heir or a Dragon just be using Scent of divine since their dont have any link with Divinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T10:58:36-07:00","id":1481937,"title":"","content":"To me it sounds more like they didn\u2019t plan on dragons when writhing Hero and they work exactly the same.<br /> <br /> To be fair, a Dragon is a Legendary Creature, while they don\u2019t have a Legend value per se, their presence in legends as something supernatural would mean their Inheritance is equivalent to Legend.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like if I create a new group, let\u2019s say fairies and say they don\u2019t have legend, but glamour, nobody can sniff them because in the book it is not written that they can specifically smell fairies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T06:15:42-07:00","id":1481988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1481937#post1481937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it sounds more like they didn\u2019t plan on dragons when writhing Hero and they work exactly the same.<br /> <br /> To be fair, a Dragon is a Legendary Creature, while they don\u2019t have a Legend value per se, their presence in legends as something supernatural would mean their Inheritance is equivalent to Legend.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like if I create a new group, let\u2019s say fairies and say they don\u2019t have legend, but glamour, nobody can sniff them because in the book it is not written that they can specifically smell fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Logic make sense, it would be good have a \u201coficial clarification\u201d on this one.<br /> <br /> What make me believe maybe their wanted adress \u201cdifferent types\u201d of Scent of dragon is the phrase \u201cUnlike heroes white sended haven been dulled\u201d.<br /> <br /> Another note, on Dragon lore their are not \u201clegendara creatures \u201c, at least defined by \u201cfate\u201d, their exist on world before de gods and the concept of \u201cfate\u201d itself exist, many of then got wraped on gods legends and became Titans or \u201cdraconic gods\u201d (Ammut,Apep,Fafnir), but when their act using their \u201clegend\u201d, their dont spawn Heirs , their spawn titanspawns or scions, Dragons even get a sort of immunity to fatebind ( it just dont stick on then).<br /> <br /> So i think i will advocate on case by case scenario, probably wont let Scent of divine work on Heirs, unless their carry something on then attached to \u201cfate\u201d like a relic or something like that, i could imagine some marvels doing the job too, maybe Order purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T06:45:35-07:00","id":1481991,"title":"","content":"I was reading it less as &quot;Heroes, being part-human, don't use this knack as effectively as heirs&quot; and more &quot;Heroes, being part human, do not have this power as an innate or automatic ability.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ymmv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T09:24:46-07:00","id":1482004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479222-dragon-scent-the-divine-dragons?p=1481991#post1481991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading it less as &amp;quot;Heroes, being part-human, don't use this knack as effectively as heirs&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;Heroes, being part human, do not have this power as an innate or automatic ability.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Ymmv</div> </div> </div> </div> Thats a way to think about it, another thing to add is,Heirs dont have it as a knack like scions (dont take knack slot and all the rules applied), its just a natural skill for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}